# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 7 ("double firings never"; a merge fires once in a tick, the left's value when both fire) and R3 (`!Updated` of a hold fires in the tick of its step, with the value after the tick): each click of "bump" reaches the hold `$total` in the click's own tick, so each row's merge hears both of its inputs and fires once, 100. Never run green.
test late_row_one_firing

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="bump")
    1: Ui.Button(label="grow")
    2/["a"]/0: Ui.Label(text="a 0: 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    2/["a"]/0: Ui.Label(text="a 1: 100")

tick 2
  in:
    1: click
  added:
    2/["b"]/0: Ui.Label(text="b 0: 0")

tick 3
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    2/["a"]/0: Ui.Label(text="a 2: 100")
    2/["b"]/0: Ui.Label(text="b 1: 100")
